# The mirror of the site through the Russian node amf (task 113,
# docs/ops/ru-node.md), for the countries where the names of
# PLUMA_SITE_DOMAINS are blocked: the same pages, the app installers and
# their updates under /dl/ (the update prefix of the desktop app and the
# update link of the iPhone app point here for those countries,
# PLUMA_RELEASES_ROUTES of bff), the iPhone app from the site and the
# links. The name points at the node, whose nginx passes the client's TLS
# as it came, behind PROXY v1, through the plumaru tunnel to port 8443 here,
# as for the edge (ru-edge.caddy): TLS ends here with home's certificate.
#
# The Caddyfile imports this file only when PLUMA_RU_SITE_DOMAIN is set
# (docker-compose.web.yaml): a site with an empty address would stop the
# whole Caddyfile. Its content is the snippets of the site in the
# Caddyfile; its server, :8443, takes PROXY v1 from the node's address in
# the tunnel only (the servers option there). A request of the node without
# the header, which would come from the node's own address, is aborted
# first, as on the edge: the services behind never see the node in place
# of a visitor.
{$PLUMA_RU_SITE_DOMAIN}:8443 {
	@unwrapped remote_ip {$PLUMA_RU_EDGE_PROXY_FROM}
	route {
		abort @unwrapped
		handle {
			import pluma_site
		}
	}
	import pluma_site_errors
}
